      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The paper is concerned with an analysis of the results of ECG daily monitoring in 60 CHD patients: 32 of them had a progressive form of unstable angina pectoris (the 1st group), and 28--stable angina pectoris (the 2nd group). Significant differences were revealed in the study groups with regard to the frequency of detection of disturbed rhythm, the total number of extrasystoles during a day, and a degree of their gradation."},
